Z||000000||mrfiero||09-02-2001||04:20 PM||||I'm still playing with my new digital camera and snapped a few shots of my 16K mile '88 GT.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackgt1.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackgt2.JPG"> <BR> <BR>Look how high the front end sits.....this is why I am considering installing lowered springs.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackgt3.JPG"> <P>The rear also sits pretty high.....this is the only real gripe I have with stock Fieros.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackgt4.JPG"> <P>Here's the odometer.....16K miles!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/16Kodo.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||LT1 Chop Top||09-02-2001||04:28 PM||||Still looks as good as it did when I saw it in Denver two years ago (onlt 14k miles then)!  Does Paul still have his 88 T-top??||||reg||14
Z||000002||mrfiero||09-02-2001||04:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LT1 Chop Top:<BR><B>Still looks as good as it did when I saw it in Denver two years ago (onlt 14k miles then)!  Does Paul still have his 88 T-top??</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I had forgotten that it was you that took the train to Rifle (I think, or was it Glenwood Springs?) to retrieve Pauls '85 GT.  <P>I need to wash and wax it again.....it's a little dusty, but it does still look good.<P>I think about the miles it would have if I didn't drive it to San Antonio right afer buying (for a Fiero show).......it would only have about 14K miles. Oh well.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>To be honest, I haven't seen or spoken to Paul in a long time, but I have talked with his dad (it's his dolly that I use on my excursions).  I do believe he still has his T-Top though.<BR>  <BR>BTW.....I'll trade you for your chop top.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tabs||09-02-2001||07:36 PM||||You only have 16k's on the car???what did u drive it 3k's every year since it was made???<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||11
Z||000004||beachbomb||09-02-2001||07:55 PM||||Very nice looking car, 16k isn't bad at all but when i saw the extra 409, well, thats way too many miles for me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>just kidding, I like it!!!<BR>jim (2 '84 Indys)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigzach_28.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000005||mrfiero||09-02-2001||09:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tabs:<BR><B>You only have 16k's on the car???what did u drive it 3k's every year since it was made???<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Only 16,409 miles!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>If I drove it 3000 miles a year since it was new I'd have 42,000 miles on her (it'll be 14 years old in October).<P>Anyways....I have only owned it for 4 years.  I bought it in 1997 with 10,019 miles.......it had been stored since early 1991, so most of the miles were put on during the first 3 years of its "life".<P>I drove it to San Antonio, TX for a Fiero show in 1998 which added over 2500 miles.  I generally drive it between 500-800 miles a year to keep everything working.<P>I just replaced the tires......the original GT+4's were getting pretty hard and dry rotted (cracked).  I scrounged up a set of new GT+4's and it drives MUCH better now.  I need to put on new shocks & struts now.     ||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||09-02-2001||09:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by beachbomb:<BR><B>Very nice looking car, 16k isn't bad at all but when i saw the extra 409, well, thats way too many miles for me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>just kidding, I like it!!!<BR>jim (2 '84 Indys)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yep.....now it's officially a "high mileage" Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||09-02-2001||11:27 PM||||16000 miles! That thing looks like it has more like 17000 on it. I will tell you what- Just sign it over to me and I will take that high mileage, crappy old Pontiac off your hands, free of charge! Just let me know when you can deliver it to the front door. <P>Great looking car MrFiero!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Galen||09-03-2001||04:56 AM||||Shoot, if I had it it'd be at 17k within a day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> dayum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I want a GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Kwez||09-03-2001||03:14 PM||||wow, great car.<P>Personally, I find the height to be just fine. (well, the front IS just a bit high maybe)<P>I like mine just like that    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ...<BR>I'm hoping that it won't be higher though when I get my new shocks !!<P>My 86 GT was a lot worst than that.<P>Are you gonna drop it w. springs or w. spindles ?<P>I just got a digi cam myself yesterday  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>my 1st camera ever !<BR>dagn this thing EATS batteries like there's non tomorrow.<P>going to take pics of my 88 today too.<p>[This message has been edited by Kwez (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||mrfiero||09-03-2001||04:58 PM||||If I didn't have other Fieros to drive it would definitley have more than 16K miles (it would be pushing 100K if I daily drove it!).   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Cooter,<P>As crappy and old as it is, I think I'll hold on to it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <BR>Kwez,<P>I probably won't lower it, but if I did I would likely just install lowered springs.  I wouldn't mind the ride height so much if the front matche the rear.....as it sits now the front is higher than the rear (almost all '88s are like this....some worse than others).<P>My digital camera also likes batteries, of course they might last longer if I would remember to turn the stupid thing off!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I think I'm going to buy some rechargables.<P>Post pics of your Fiero as soon as you can!<P><BR>BTW......by next summer my baby will have almost 18K miles.  I plan on driving it to the national show in Missouri next summer.||||reg||1
