Z||000012||Kwez||09-03-2001||05:48 PM||||Dagn, you ARE right, <BR>the front is too high compared to the rear ... <BR>I did think the rear was too low before compared to my prev 86GT, but now I would say the rear is ok, the front is too low.<BR>check here: <A HREF="http://www.enter-net.com/~pquesnel/car/fiero/Red_86GT/original/Phil04-ok.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.enter-net.com/~pquesnel/car/fiero/Red_86GT/original/Phil04-ok.jpg</A> <P>here are the pics I took today : <A HREF="http://www.enter-net.com/~pquesnel/car/fiero/white_88GT/Index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.enter-net.com/~pquesnel/car/fiero/white_88GT/Index.html</A> <P>hmmm, I guess I'll need some practice, my photographer skills aren't what they could be   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>(I'll use this excuse for the quality: I bought the cheapest digi cam i could find ;-)<P>I just noticed the white GT on top of the board, I guess that's what it would look like lowered.<p>[This message has been edited by Kwez (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000013||fiero56||09-03-2001||07:18 PM||||The cool thing about stock '88 ride heught is when your on the throttle, it appears the front end is lifting to by-standers <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.||||reg||1
Z||000014||starfighter007@msn.com||09-03-2001||08:11 PM||||Ill have to agree with Cooter after closer examination of the pictures you posted Im thinking 17000.miles to I mean you could have doctored them pics.If you you want to unload that heap that sits waaaaaay to high up in the air Ill do you a favor and take it off your hands.Only because your a forum member in what I believe to be in good standings. Ill even give you shall we say $75.00 And remember she does sit high and not to mention that high mileage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||mrfiero||09-03-2001||08:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>The cool thing about stock '88 ride heught is when your on the throttle, it appears the front end is lifting to by-standers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>That reminds me of a yellow GT way back in 1994.  It was at the national show in Indianapolis and the Sunday after the show was an SCCA type of race.  This yellow GT was stock, but had HUGE tires (I guess he thought it looked good?)......anyways, it was a 5-sp. and everytime he laucnhed it at the start or gunned it out of a corner the front end lifted really high.  It was a sight to see.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000016||mrfiero||09-03-2001||08:45 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by starfighter007@msn.com:<BR><B>Ill have to agree with Cooter after closer examination of the pictures you posted Im thinking 17000.miles to I mean you could have doctored them pics.If you you want to unload that heap that sits waaaaaay to high up in the air Ill do you a favor and take it off your hands.Only because your a forum member in what I believe to be in good standings. Ill even give you shall we say $75.00 And remember she does sit high and not to mention that high mileage    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Doctored?  I wish I knew enough about this photo shop program to do that......then I would have cleaned it up a bit.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you look close at the close-up of the front wheel you will see a section of paint that is missing from the fenders lower ground effect.  It flew off as I was washing it one day.  The reason?  Mudflaps!  The original owner had mudflaps on it (I took them off) and the result was several holes on the inside of the fenderwell and on the little ground effect thing.  I guess this compromised the integrity of the paint and it just peeled off (it's now a gray patch).  I bought new moldings, but it will cost about $75 to paint them plus I have to disassemble the inner fenderwell as well as the fender itself (read big PITA).<P>At any rate, Starfighter, I will "file" your offer in the appropriate receptical and will get back to you.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>I have $75, do I hear $100??    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||1
